Today I officially submitted my report, marking the end of my **3-month internship at the National Institute for Materials Science (NIMS)** in **Tsukuba, Japan**.

It was an amazing experience, and I am very grateful for the opportunity to be hosted there. **Professor Naoto Shirahata** and the **nanoparticle group** welcomed me with open arms and made my time in Japan not only productive, but genuinely memorable.

This internship provided valuable hands-on research experience and helped strengthen international collaborations, which will directly inform the next stage of my PhD work.

I am very much looking forward to returning in the future. For now, my focus is on completing my **PhD at the University of Bristol** and turning this work into a publication.

Thank you to everyone who made this experience so rewarding.

